# Files and directories kept out of the release ZIP.
#
# `make package` copies the tree with `rsync --exclude-from=.distignore`, so
# these are rsync patterns: a leading slash anchors to the package root, and an
# unanchored rule matches at any depth. Anchor every directory rule: the editor
# under dist/static/ has its own themes/ and vendor/ folders (built-in styles,
# the TinyMCE theme, the SCORM 1.2 runtime), and an unanchored `themes/` once
# shipped packages whose editor previews and screenshots had no style.
#
# The bundled editor under dist/static/ is a release artifact and must stay in
# the package -- see ADR-28-01. Do not add a `dist` rule here.
#
# `make build-editor` also drops a local symlink at asset/static -> ../dist/static
# so Omeka can serve the same tree during development. zip follows that symlink
# unless -y is passed, so leaving it in the staging tree ships the editor twice
# (~2x the ZIP). Exclude the symlink; runtime loads dist/static/ only.

# VCS and CI
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.distignore

# Agent instructions and skills. Skills live in .agents/skills/, with
# .claude/skills/ symlinking to them; neither belongs in a published module.
.agents
.claude
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
# rsync matches names case-sensitively, and the pointer was once tracked as
# claude.md; a macOS checkout can keep that spelling on disk after the rename.
claude.md

# Editor and local tooling leftovers
.aider*
.DS_Store
.env
.env.dist
.playwright-mcp
node_modules

# Build inputs. Only the built editor in dist/static/ ships; the editor
# checkout it is built from does not. The asset/static symlink is local-only
# (see the header comment); asset/css, asset/js and asset/thumbnails do ship.
/exelearning/
/asset/static
/vendor/
/themes/

# Tests, their caches, and the coverage reports they write
/test/
/test/.phpunit.result.cache
/test/.phpunit.cache/
/artifacts/

# Development tooling and configuration. scripts/ holds the architecture-record
# validator: a documentation linter, not module code.
/scripts/
/architecture-records.json
/.editor-version
phpmd.xml
codecov.yml
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
composer.json
composer.lock
blueprint.json
renovate.json

# Development data for `make up`/`make seed` and the Playground blueprint (which
# fetches the fixture from GitHub, not from the package). data/ itself ships:
# data/nginx-exelearning.conf is the server snippet the README tells admins to use.
/data/fixtures/
/data/*.csv
/data/seed-exelearning.sh

# Translation sources. Omeka loads language/*.mo only (config/module.config.php).
/language/*.po
/language/*.pot

# Repository documentation and local analysis. docs/ holds the architecture
# records, not user docs.
/docs/
/analysis/
/legacy/

# Packaging output
*.zip
